# Omarchy migrations reviewed for Ubuntu, one per line: <name> run|skip  # reason
#
#   run   omarchy-migrate runs it at Hyprland login, with the layer first on PATH and no terminal. Only for
#         migrations that edit user config or state (never sudo, /etc, packages, mise or Arch-only hardware:
#         sudo has no terminal to ask in, and a failure holds back every migration after it), and that leave
#         a config that is already current as it is: an install from before omarchy-migrate ran migrations
#         gets every run entry newer than layer/migrations.baseline, whatever version its configs came from.
#   skip  omarchy-migrate marks it done without running it.
#
# A migration that isn't listed stays pending, and omarchy-migrate warns about it; tools/check-migrations
# fails on it. Omarchy's order is by file name, and so is this list's.

# ---- v4.5.0 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1786609204 skip  # Only prints a message.
1786719479 skip  # Gemini -> Antigravity: installs agy through mise, which the port doesn't set up.
1786967403 skip  # mise wrapper (Kimi); the port doesn't set up mise.
